+    return f'''<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+<title>{escape(title)} · Cafe Replenishment</title><meta name="description" content="{escape(description, quote=True)}">
+<link rel="canonical" href="{escape(SITE_ORIGIN + path, quote=True)}"><meta property="og:url" content="{escape(SITE_ORIGIN + path, quote=True)}"><meta property="og:title" content="{escape(title + ' · Cafe Replenishment', quote=True)}"><meta property="og:type" content="website">
+<meta name="theme-color" content="#264f3e"><meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
+<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/assets/mark.svg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/language.css"><script type="module" src="/assets/language.js"></script></head>
+<body class="public-single-language"><a class="skip" href="#main">{pair('Skip to content','跳到内容')}</a><header><div class="wrap nav"><a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/assets/mark.svg" width="42" height="42" alt=""><span>Cafe Replenishment<small>{pair('KUALA LUMPUR DEMO','明日备货 · 吉隆坡演示')}</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Website navigation" data-aria-en="Website navigation" data-aria-zh="网站导航">{nav}<button type="button" class="language-settings" data-language-settings>Settings</button></nav></div></header>
+{body}
+<footer><div class="wrap footer-inner"><span>{pair('Cafe Replenishment · Independently developed demonstration project','Cafe Replenishment · 独立开发的演示项目')}</span><div class="footer-links"><a href="/demo/">{pair('Try the demo','体验演示')}</a><a href="/privacy/">{pair('Privacy policy','隐私政策')}</a><a href="/terms/">{pair('Terms of use','使用条款')}</a><a href="/privacy/#contact">{pair('Contact','联系')}</a></div></div></footer></body></html>'''
+
+home = '''<main id="main">
+<section class="wrap hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">A little clarity before closing</p><h1>A calmer close.<br><em>A better prepared<br>morning.</em></h1><p class="lead">Bring tomorrow’s forecast, today’s stock and your own judgement together. Cafe Replenishment helps café owners review a practical shopping list, then prepare supplier drafts.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#workflow">See how it works ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">How your data is used</a></div><p class="micro">A local desktop demonstration using synthetic sales and inventory. Purchasing decisions remain with the owner.</p></div>
+<div class="board" aria-label="Illustrative replenishment review" data-aria-en="Illustrative replenishment review" data-aria-zh="补货核对示例"><div class="board-inner"><div class="board-top"><div><span class="micro">TOMORROW’S PREPARATION</span><strong>Ready for your review</strong></div><span class="pill">Illustrative demo</span></div><div class="context"><div>Weather context<b>Rain may change demand</b></div><div>Calendar context<b>Check local holidays</b></div></div><table class="demo-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Ingredient</th><th scope="col">Suggested packs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fresh milk</td><td><b>15 boxes</b></td></tr><tr><td>Oat milk</td><td><b>7 cartons</b></td></tr><tr><td>Coffee beans</td><td><b>3 bags</b></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="board-note">Review quantities → Approve the list → Create supplier drafts<br>Example quantities only. No live purchasing takes place on this website.</div></div></div></section>
+<div class="wrap band"><span>Weather &amp; holiday context</span><span>Owner review before procurement</span><span>Supplier drafts, ready to check</span></div>
+<section id="workflow" class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">From closing time to opening time</p><h2>Four steps. One considered<br>decision.</h2><div class="steps"><article><span class="step-num">01</span><h3>Understand tomorrow</h3><p>The local app combines demo sales, stock, recipes and selected weather and holiday context to estimate demand.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">02</span><h3>Review the shopping list</h3><p>Ingredients are converted into purchasable packs. The owner can adjust quantities and inspect any resulting shortfall.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">03</span><h3>Approve with confidence</h3><p>The owner confirms the list in the local or phone workbench. Approval creates a recorded procurement draft.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">04</span><h3>Prepare supplier drafts</h3><p>With optional Gmail authorization, approved drafts can be saved in the owner’s Gmail drafts folder. The owner decides whether to send.</p></article></div></section>
+<section class="data-section"><div class="wrap section split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Clear boundaries for your data</p><h2>Your workbench stays<br>on your computer.</h2><p>This public website explains the project. The replenishment workbench, purchasing records and Google authorization credentials are managed by the locally installed application.</p><p>Google authorization begins from that local workbench. This site has no token-entry form, sales-data upload or procurement controls.</p><a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read the complete privacy policy →</a></div><ul class="data-list"><li><span>↗</span><div><strong>Gmail is optional</strong><p>Connect your own account to save approved procurement drafts. Access tokens can refresh when needed.</p></div></li><li><span>✓</span><div><strong>Only the necessary Google permission</strong><p>The app requests gmail.compose. Google defines this as managing drafts and sending email; this implementation creates drafts and checks connectivity.</p></div></li><li><span>↶</span><div><strong>You can disconnect</strong><p>Clear local authorization in the workbench or revoke access in your Google Account. Existing Gmail drafts remain until you delete them.</p></div></li></ul></div></section>
+<section class="wrap index-note"><div><h3>A demonstration, with honest limits.</h3><p>Sales and inventory examples are synthetic. Forecast accuracy for a real café has not been validated. Weather data and optional cloud inference require their respective services; owner approval remains essential.</p></div><div lang="zh-CN"><h3>明日备货，让收店前的决定更清楚。</h3><p>在本机工作台查看天气与假日影响，按包装修改采购量，确认后生成供应商草稿。公开网站用于项目介绍和政策披露；演示采用模拟数据，采购由老板最终决定。</p></div></section></main>'''
+
+privacy = f'''<p class="doc-intro">This policy explains the difference between this informational website and the locally operated Cafe Replenishment application, including its optional Gmail connection.</p>
+<p class="updated">Effective date: 22 October 2026 · Application: Cafe Replenishment</p>
+<h2 id="operator">1. The project and this website</h2><p>Cafe Replenishment is an independently maintained café replenishment demonstration project. The public website provides an overview, this privacy policy and terms. It does not provide an application account, receive sales or inventory uploads, collect OAuth credentials, or operate the local replenishment workbench.</p><p>The hosting provider may process ordinary request information such as IP addresses, browser information, access logs or platform session data. The site does not add its own advertising trackers or analytics scripts.</p>
+<h2 id="local">2. Information in the local application</h2><p>The application currently uses synthetic sales and inventory for demonstrations. On the operator’s computer it stores recipes, ingredient stock, supplier contact details, demand forecasts, procurement lists, approval history, supplier draft contents and API export status. The operator controls this local runtime directory.</p>
+<h2 id="gmail">3. Google information and Gmail permissions</h2><p>Connecting Gmail is optional and begins from the local owner workbench. The application requests <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.compose</code>. This Google permission includes managing drafts and sending email. The current application uses it to check connectivity and create procurement drafts; it has no email-sending operation.</p><p>A connection check requests a list containing at most one draft’s identifiers. It does not fetch message bodies. Creating a draft submits the owner-approved supplier recipient, email subject and message body to Google. Gmail returns draft and message identifiers, which are stored locally with export status. The application does not import the inbox or read received email content.</p>
+<h2 id="credentials">4. Authorization credentials and automatic refresh</h2><p>OAuth client credentials, access tokens and refresh tokens are stored by the local server. On Windows they are protected using current-user DPAPI. Other supported platforms use a file with restricted permissions; this is not described as encryption. Credentials are not returned to the phone workbench, embedded in this website, included in supplier messages, or intentionally recorded in application logs.</p><p>When needed for a connection check or draft creation, the local server sends the refresh token to Google’s token service to obtain an access token. Authorization is not permanent: Google test-mode limits, revocation, password changes or account policies may require another browser authorization. The owner can configure service credentials through environment variables; those overrides are managed separately.</p>
+<h2 id="sharing">5. Other services and AI processing</h2><p>If enabled, Runpod receives selected forecasting inputs: product identifiers, demand estimates, permitted adjustment limits and selected weather and holiday context. The current application does not send Google-derived Gmail information, Google OAuth credentials, supplier contacts or procurement email bodies to Runpod, and does not use Google user data to train AI models.</p><p>Weather requests use the configured city or coordinates with the weather provider. A WhatsApp prefilled link includes the supplier phone number and draft text when the owner opens that link. Sending a WhatsApp message remains the owner’s action. Google, Runpod, the weather provider and WhatsApp process submitted information under their own policies.</p>
+<h2 id="limited-use">6. Google API Limited Use</h2><p>Cafe Replenishment’s use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements. Google user data is used to provide the requested Gmail draft functionality. It is not sold, used for advertising, or used to train generalized AI models.</p>
+<h2 id="retention">7. Retention, disconnection and deletion</h2><p>Local procurement and approval records remain in the runtime directory until the operator deletes them. Successful draft identifiers and export statuses remain so the application can avoid duplicate creation. There is no scheduled automatic purge.</p><p>“Disconnect Gmail” attempts to revoke the Google authorization and clears locally saved access and refresh tokens. It retains desktop client settings, local procurement records and draft content. If Google revocation cannot be confirmed, the workbench reports that uncertainty. Credentials supplied by environment variables must also be removed from the launch environment.</p><p>You can revoke the application from <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google Account third-party connections</a>. Revocation does not delete drafts already saved in Gmail. Delete those in Gmail, and remove local records from the runtime directory when no longer needed. Close the local server before deleting its runtime files.</p>
+<h2 id="contact">8. Contact and policy changes</h2><p>{CONTACT}</p><p>Policy changes will be reflected on this page with an updated effective date. Material changes to how the application uses Google data require an updated disclosure and any authorization required by Google.</p><div class="notice" lang="zh-CN">中文摘要：网站只介绍项目；库存与采购记录保留在本机。Gmail 授权用于检查连接和创建已审批草稿；Google 权限本身包含发送能力，但当前程序没有发送操作。Google 数据与令牌不用于 AI 训练。你可以在工作台断开授权，并到 Google 账户撤销；已生成草稿需在 Gmail 中自行删除。</div>'''
+
+terms = f'''<p class="doc-intro">These terms describe the intended use and practical limits of the Cafe Replenishment demonstration and its informational website.</p><p class="updated">Effective date: 22 October 2026 · Application: Cafe Replenishment</p>
+<h2 id="purpose">1. Intended use</h2><p>Cafe Replenishment is an independently maintained software demonstration for forecasting café demand, reviewing replenishment quantities and preparing supplier drafts. It currently uses synthetic demonstration sales and stock records. It is not a validated production inventory, accounting or purchasing service.</p>
+<h2 id="review">2. Owner review and purchasing</h2><p>The owner is responsible for verifying stock counts, recipes, units, pack sizes, supplier details, prices, delivery arrangements and expiry dates before purchasing. Forecasts, weather context and holiday effects are estimates. They do not guarantee future demand, ingredient availability, cost savings or business outcomes.</p><p>Approving a list creates procurement records and local supplier drafts. Saving to Gmail creates a draft, not a supplier order or payment. Opening a WhatsApp prefilled link does not establish that a message was sent or a supplier accepted an order.</p>
+<h2 id="accounts">3. Accounts, credentials and services</h2><p>Use only accounts and service credentials you are authorized to use. The application’s Google connection is optional and requires your consent. You are responsible for access to the local computer and workbench and for protecting service credentials. Never publish access tokens, refresh tokens, client secrets or the private runtime directory.</p><p>Google, Runpod, weather and messaging services may have their own terms, quotas, availability limits and fees. Optional Runpod inference may incur charges. This website does not purchase domains, compute capacity, ingredients or supplier services on your behalf.</p>
+<h2 id="availability">4. Availability and limitations</h2><p>The demonstration is provided as available, without a promise of uninterrupted service, forecast accuracy or suitability for a particular shop. Review outputs before relying on them. Local scheduled checks require the application’s server to remain running. A website deployment or Gmail connection does not itself validate the forecasting model.</p>
+<h2 id="privacy">5. Privacy and access control</h2><p>Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> before connecting Google or another service. The public website is separate from the local workbench and does not expose your inventory, approval records or OAuth credentials. Disconnecting an integration does not erase existing procurement records or Gmail drafts.</p>
+<h2 id="responsible-use">6. Responsible use and changes</h2><p>Do not use the application to access another person’s account without permission, evade service restrictions or send unwanted messages. The project may change or discontinue features. These terms do not override rights or obligations that cannot be excluded under applicable law.</p>
